      "actual_observations": [
        "Both exact derived selections were played fully at1x against their actual song placements, early[6,102) at83.083333–87.083333s and late[102,214) at254.625–259.291667s. The two consecutive source portions are not looped or retimed. Both launches exclude--mute-audio and both complete with0drops/errors/stalls/corruption.",
        "All208 used derived frames were inspected in chronological framing sheets and all208 native lower-right corner crops. The old invented corner glyph is entirely outside this fixed rectangle. This is a deliberate full-shot reframing, with no paint/mask or in-shot concealment of a prop-contact defect.",
        "Eyes, nose, jaw, shoulders, both connected wrists and functional fretting/picking contacts remain inside the crop throughout the208 used frames. The low picking stroke raw110–134 was additionally inspected at native crop scale: the y44 rectangle retains the fingertips that the rejected y22 candidate would have cut.",
        "The portrait intentionally crops part of the hair crown and the headstock/tuner tip can naturally cross the right frame edge during the late rise, including raw178. Do not claim that all six tuners are visible in every derived frame. Headstock motion is continuous and is not a tool morph; original source hardware/contact review remains retained.",
        "The original consecutively reviewed playing pixels survive losslessly. Early compact picking/fretting reads as restrained playing. In the late actual-song context the touches grow gentler, shoulder effort reduces and she lifts her attention as if listening; no broad vigorous strumming, triumphant pose or frozen still is introduced.",
        "Same blonde female guitarist, lace/asymmetric black outfit, neutral ornament, guitar/strap and stage. No cross, extra limb or ghost person is introduced by this deterministic crop. Brief original native finger-line softness around raw98–100/169–171 remains scoped motion texture, not newly repaired sharp anatomy."
      ],
